% ============================================================================
% roman-numerals.query.adj — a worked recall over the mathematics Roman library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is the value of X?":
% it states no arithmetic fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table
% and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `roman_numeral_value` rows and returns the value + the table's source/locator/
% trust. A letter that is not a Roman symbol abstains honestly — the engine never
% invents a value.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli roman-numerals.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "roman-numerals.adj"

? roman_numeral_value(x, $V)           % expect 10
? roman_numeral_value(m, $V)           % expect 1000
? roman_numeral_value($S, 50)          % reverse recall — expect $S = l
? roman_numeral_value(q, $V)           % expect abstain — q is not a Roman numeral
